// node mutation.mjs [pattern]        e.g.  node mutation.mjs search     (only mutations whose name contains "search")
//
// The receipt that a test guards a behaviour: put the defect BACK into today's code and require a red suite. Each line below changes one
// thing in one file, runs `node --test` from the repository root, and says KILLED (the suite failed: the behaviour is guarded) or
// SURVIVED (it passed: nothing guards that line, or the line is a shortcut). A mutation whose text is no longer in the file says
// STALE, so a refactor cannot make this script quietly pass. Every file is put back after each run, and again if the script is stopped.
// The BASELINE (the suite run first, with no mutation) must be green: ANY red test, an empty run or an unrecognized report aborts the whole
// script with exit 2 (INCONCLUSIVE, line ~1374); red tests are NOT ignored (corrected 27/10/2026: this header said they were, which was true of the runner on main until the film-page change of 24/10/2026).
// A mutation is KILLED only by a test that was green in the baseline, so one red test somewhere else cannot "kill" every mutation.
//
// 24/10/2026: selects spec reporter and concurrency 1 explicitly, including on Node 22.
// A non-green/unrecognized/empty baseline aborts. Named newly-red assertions are required;
// import, syntax and process timeout failures are INCONCLUSIVE, never accepted as kills.

